<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85428" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολῠτί̄μ-ητος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολῠτῑμ-τίμᾱτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Pax</u>
			978
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμάω</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>highly honoured,</i> freq. used
			in addressing a divinity, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀφροδίτη</span> [<i><span class="en">
				Parm.
			</span></i>]<i><span class="en">
				20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ Ζεῦ πολυτίμητ᾽</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pherecr.
					73
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				319
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ πολυτίμηθ᾽ Ἠράκλεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					807
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ π. θεοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>V.</u>
					1001
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεώ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					594
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ π. Νεφέλαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					269
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ π. Αἰσχύλε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					851
				</span></i>
			; and (ironically) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ π. Εὐθύδημε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Euthd.</u>
					296d
				</span></i>
			; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π. ἰατρεῖον,</span> of
			Aristotle, <i><span class="en">
				Timae.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				12.8.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>at a high price, very costly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				387.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Trall.
				1.15
			</span></i>; with play on signf. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῖτος] π. ᾇπερ τοὶ θεοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					759
				</span></i>
			.</div>
